# Cashtrix environment
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Expo only exposes EXPO_PUBLIC_* to
# the bundle — never put the service role key here (that lives in Edge
# Functions only, PRD §4.4).

# Publishable (anon) key for project `Cashtrix` — safe in the bundle, RLS is
# the actual guard. Get it from the Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Sentry DSN (V1, issue #30) — optional. Empty = the redacted in-memory buffer
# from T10 stays in place (daily Expo Go work). Set it in `.env` for local
# dev-client runs, or as an EAS secret for preview/production builds; the
# release channel then reports crashes with `amount`/`note` scrubbed.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
